{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01356",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 1.35,
      "end_seconds": 8.14,
      "duration_seconds": 6.79,
      "text": "Doctor, this one's ready for you. Everything's on the chart, but I'll go through it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 9.18,
      "end_seconds": 14.04,
      "duration_seconds": 4.86,
      "text": "Thanks. Hello, come in, sit down. What brings you in today?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 16.09,
      "end_seconds": 21.27,
      "duration_seconds": 5.18,
      "text": "Um, so... skipped beats. That's why I came."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 22.71,
      "end_seconds": 26.75,
      "duration_seconds": 4.04,
      "text": "Okay, can you tell me when it first started?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 28.57,
      "end_seconds": 46.25,
      "duration_seconds": 17.68,
      "text": "Um, uh, I'd say ten days. Actually, no, closer to about four days. I'm not great at remembering details, so bear with me. I thought it would sort itself out, but it hasn't."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 46.72,
      "end_seconds": 56.16,
      "duration_seconds": 9.44,
      "text": "Yes. Can you describe it a bit more for me? How strong it is, what the pattern is, what helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 59.62,
      "end_seconds": 87.57,
      "duration_seconds": 27.95,
      "text": "Hmm, only deep breaths, and it's not much. It just comes and goes. It's worse with lying down and caffeine. Sorry, what was I saying, as for being a bit anxious, I honestly can't say when that began. It might have been last month or the month before."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 88.53,
      "end_seconds": 92.85,
      "duration_seconds": 4.32,
      "text": "Has there been a flutter in your chest too?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 93.58,
      "end_seconds": 95.53,
      "duration_seconds": 1.95,
      "text": "Yes, I have."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 97.54,
      "end_seconds": 100.38,
      "duration_seconds": 2.84,
      "text": "Do you have any chronic illnesses?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 102.02,
      "end_seconds": 105.71,
      "duration_seconds": 3.69,
      "text": "I have migraines, for about a year."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 107.16,
      "end_seconds": 118.48,
      "duration_seconds": 11.32,
      "text": "I follow. Right, so migraines is already on your record. We'll keep that in mind today. Are there any illnesses in your family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 119.77,
      "end_seconds": 122.87,
      "duration_seconds": 3.1,
      "text": "My mother has an underactive thyroid."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 124.08,
      "end_seconds": 127.84,
      "duration_seconds": 3.76,
      "text": "Do you take any prescribed or over-the-counter medicines?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 129.84,
      "end_seconds": 144.57,
      "duration_seconds": 14.73,
      "text": "I take sumatriptan, 50 milligrams, when needed. Actually, I'm supposed to take it regularly, but I don't always manage. Herbal calming tea. I take it in the evening."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 146.6,
      "end_seconds": 151.95,
      "duration_seconds": 5.35,
      "text": "Has anything ever caused you a reaction? I mean any allergies."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 153.47,
      "end_seconds": 157.13,
      "duration_seconds": 3.66,
      "text": "Mm, no, I'm not allergic to anything."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 174.68,
      "end_seconds": 177.02,
      "duration_seconds": 2.34,
      "text": "Now some background about your lifestyle."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 181.5,
      "end_seconds": 206.5,
      "duration_seconds": 25.0,
      "text": "I used to drink heavily but I stopped four years ago. No, I've never smoked in my life. I walk the dog every morning. I work in accounts at a hospital. I drink a lot of tea and snack through the day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 224.61,
      "end_seconds": 229.79,
      "duration_seconds": 5.18,
      "text": "A few quick ones: fainting, chest pain, shortness of breath or dizziness?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 234.96,
      "end_seconds": 241.23,
      "duration_seconds": 6.27,
      "text": "No, uh, no fainting, chest pain, shortness of breath or dizziness."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 242.22,
      "end_seconds": 243.58,
      "duration_seconds": 1.36,
      "text": "Neurologically, anything strange?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 245.68,
      "end_seconds": 247.39,
      "duration_seconds": 1.71,
      "text": "Nothing odd there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 249.27,
      "end_seconds": 251.65,
      "duration_seconds": 2.38,
      "text": "Alright, how's your breathing otherwise?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 252.42,
      "end_seconds": 257.78,
      "duration_seconds": 5.36,
      "text": "I mean, um, no, my breathing's been fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 258.94,
      "end_seconds": 270.57,
      "duration_seconds": 11.63,
      "text": "Doctor, I've got the readings for you. Pulse 73, respiratory rate 17, blood pressure 123 over 71, oxygen saturation is 97 percent, temperature 36.5."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 272.04,
      "end_seconds": 273.5,
      "duration_seconds": 1.46,
      "text": "Good, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 275.09,
      "end_seconds": 278.34,
      "duration_seconds": 3.25,
      "text": "Could you come over to the couch, please?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 279.44,
      "end_seconds": 281.68,
      "duration_seconds": 2.24,
      "text": "Tell me if that's sore."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 299.53,
      "end_seconds": 303.53,
      "duration_seconds": 4.0,
      "text": "Your pulse is regular and your heart sounds are normal."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 307.55,
      "end_seconds": 310.77,
      "duration_seconds": 3.22,
      "text": "Alright, that's all I needed to check."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 322.4,
      "end_seconds": 330.5,
      "duration_seconds": 8.1,
      "text": "Okay, so my impression is this: This is probably harmless extra heartbeats. I'd also keep an anxiety-related palpitation in mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 331.03,
      "end_seconds": 335.27,
      "duration_seconds": 4.24,
      "text": "Let me think, is this serious, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 336.9,
      "end_seconds": 356.23,
      "duration_seconds": 19.33,
      "text": "Nothing I've seen today points to an emergency. It looks like harmless extra heartbeats, but I'd like to confirm. Let me just check I've got this right. You've had skipped beats for about four days, and no fainting or shortness of breath."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 357.23,
      "end_seconds": 360.9,
      "duration_seconds": 3.67,
      "text": "Well, uh, yes, you've got it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 362.83,
      "end_seconds": 368.93,
      "duration_seconds": 6.1,
      "text": "Doctor, I did an ECG before they came in, the result's on your screen."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 369.49,
      "end_seconds": 379.67,
      "duration_seconds": 10.18,
      "text": "Thanks, I'll have a look. There's nothing new for me to start or arrange today. Have I covered everything you wanted?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 380.42,
      "end_seconds": 383.79,
      "duration_seconds": 3.37,
      "text": "Hmm, thank you, that's helpful."
    }
  ]
}